---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LightSim from '../components/islands/LightSim.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Light Lab" description="A spectral light tracer: a beam rakes across a darkened table through glass, refracting by wavelength and fading by Beer–Lambert.">
  <article class="concept">
    <h1>Light Lab</h1>
    <p class="summary">
      Turn the room lights down and rake a slit of light across the table. Every ray carries one
      wavelength, bends by that wavelength's refractive index, and fades inside coloured glass by
      that wavelength's absorption. The colours you see are the sum of a million such rays.
    </p>
    <LightSim />
    <p>
      Two things to try. With the dense flint prism, the white beam fans into a spectrum, because
      the index falls from 1.83 at 420 nm to 1.77 at 700 nm. With crown glass the fan is
      about a quarter as wide (its index falls only from 1.528 to 1.513). Then give the prism cobalt and drag it up
      and down: light crossing the thin apex keeps more red than light crossing the thick base,
      because absorption grows with path length. The glass has no single colour; each ray's colour
      depends on how far it travelled through it.
    </p>
    <p class="back"><a href={`${base}/`}>← back to the start</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
